    requirement: Capture native voltage and current through rising, falling and repeated
    pulses.

    General teaching principle: Electrical measurements are differences
    or flows that require a correct reference, operating condition and fresh solver
    evidence.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this
    objective is complete.'
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
